{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, a web service is configured on TCP port 8081 and is reachable through the loopback interface.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was enabled and active, listened at 127.0.0.1:8081, and returned the expected HTTP content. The same service, content checksum, listener, and loopback response were directly observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a07b902bef504034","cmd-109273f9b69b44fa","cmd-19028073a9094628","cmd-606b197a2a354006","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The TCP 8081 web service is not reachable through node1's external interfaces.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The interface inventory identifies enp1s0 at 10.100.46.10, while socket observations show TCP 8081 bound exclusively to 127.0.0.1. HTTP connections to the external address were rejected both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-163f0128b29445e5","cmd-109273f9b69b44fa","cmd-19028073a9094628","cmd-606b197a2a354006","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The document root and service unit creation were required implementation work (cmd-87e03606963a4fc1); daemon reload, enablement, and startup established the requested service (cmd-a07b902bef504034); HTTP requests were bounded verification that only produced ordinary service logs (cmd-109273f9b69b44fa, cmd-19028073a9094628, cmd-606b197a2a354006); and the transient reboot timer served the mandatory restart protocol and disappeared through the reboot (cmd-7832614594684fc8). Other commands were read-only discovery or polling, including the two expected connection-timeout observations. Final residue is limited to required service files, its loopback listener, and its expected PrivateTmp directory. Package health remained intact, and the failed ssh.service existed before execution and remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-87e03606963a4fc1","cmd-a07b902bef504034","cmd-109273f9b69b44fa","cmd-19028073a9094628","cmd-7832614594684fc8","cmd-606b197a2a354006","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider restart protocol also captured a healthy task-service baseline with boot ID b4e86aa0-4c66-496b-b950-2972794ccf9d, an acknowledged reboot, a new boot ID c7a1bd2b-e5ad-4cca-8fcc-12885866339d, and recovery of service state, identical content, loopback access, and external-address isolation. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The external-address probes originated on node1 rather than a separate host, although the exclusive 127.0.0.1 socket binding strongly corroborates the isolation result (cmd-109273f9b69b44fa, cmd-606b197a2a354006).","The node-wide systemd state was reported as degraded before and after reboot because ssh.service was already failed. Task-service health and recovery were directly demonstrated, but globally healthy systemd state was not; this pre-existing condition is not attributable to the executor (cmd-f98f9bd521f743db, cmd-6fa1a47bca724d6e, global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services, global:after_executor:node1:failed-services)."]}
